## Prefill fetch

Tool output prefilled with a top-128 fetch per chunk: fetch_all +0.0165 vs fetch_all_noprefill +0.0405; difference -0.0240 [-0.0394, -0.0117] (negative = the prefill fetch lifts the ceiling). Prefill fetch moves 84.1 MB per turn on average (0.043 of the bf16 history).

## Bytes

Per pause on average: bf16 history 2,243 MB; resident int1 0.138 and int2 0.200 of bf16; uniform int2's one-time extra reload over int1: 139 MB (0.062 of bf16).

Moved per turn = bytes fetched at every step, summed over the turn's steps (no reuse across steps). Unique per turn = distinct (layer, head, token) pairs fetched over the turn (what a fetch cache would move). Both are shown as MB and as a multiple of int2's one-time extra reload on the same pause. Resident = int1 history + one step's fetched set, as a fraction of bf16, next to resident int2. spec also decodes one speculative token per step (compute, not bytes). Prefill-fetch bytes are not included here (see Prefill fetch).

